  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The vast majority of avatars people use are \"very poor\". Often, I'll be at a 60+ person party and practically everyone has \"very poor\" avatars. My safety settings will filter out the worst offenders and instead render their fallback avatar. That's great, but then everyone at the party is either using a horribly unoptimized avatar, or an extremely optimized avatar. There's no middle ground. Visually, there's a huge difference between the two. I'd much rather see a PC Green avatar than a fallback avatar. Fallback avatars are _very_ limited, but most people have a decent looking PC Green avatar on hand. \nTDLR: Please add the option to use a \"PC Green\" avatar as a fallback avatar",
